WEBVTT

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:43.880
Batting first: shortstop, Shimizu-kun.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.340
Play ball!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.570
It's finally starting.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.010
Even Kaido's second string is strong, right?

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.910
Strike!

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.120
I-It's fast!

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.620
This is Kaido?

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.470
<i>Enomoto?</i>

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.590
Strike!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.850
As expected of you, Shimizu.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.280
How cocky of you to even scratch it as a first-year.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.560
Same with you, Baba-senpai.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.470
Although you're on the second string, you're Kaido's regular catcher...

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.820
You're the pride of the Yokohama Little's old boys.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.760
Why didn't you come to Kaido?

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.620
Strike! Batter out!

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.350
I guess it's impossible.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.300
After all...

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.110
since my abilities are only of this level...

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.010
I just chose whatever was the closest to my home.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.610
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.650
Hey, Taiga.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:34.500
Yeah?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.360
Do you... know that pitcher?

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.710
Strike!

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.650
Are you talking about Enomoto's little brother?

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.850
Little brother?

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:49.370
Yeah.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:53.930
He's the little brother of Enomoto, Kaido's ace last year.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.930
Strike!

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.990
They're really famous siblings.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.480
Strike! Batter out!

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.430
<i>No wonder their looks and pitching styles are alike.</i>

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.410
Strike! Batter out!

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.110
Change!

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.900
They easily struck out three batters!

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.140
Even if they're the second string, they're still Kaido.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.420
They're not an opponent we can compete against in the first place.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.270
Egashira-san...

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.840
Why do we have to play against these kinds of guys?

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.530
Just last year, he was a member of our baseball team.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.580
He defeated the main team at last year's intramural game.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.800
T-The main team?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:18.970
With this... you should feel a little more enthusiastic, right?

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.410
Batting first: right fielder, Uotani-kun. {I think the name should be checked with the manga}{Jez: Name's the same as that in the manga.}

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.640
Play.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.730
<i>Please be careful.</i>

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.390
<i>The reason for this game is probably because Egashira is targeting you.</i>

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.150
<i>Bring it on.</i>

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.570
<i>If you can... </i>

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.860
<i>just try and trick me!</i>

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.820
Strike!

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.010
Strike!

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:02.000
It seems fast.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.360
It seems that it's true that he was at our school.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.880
But...

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.090
he only has fastballs.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.060
Foul!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:16.540
H-He hit it...

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.770
H-He hit it...

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:20.920
And...

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.030
his team's fielders are like trash.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.370
Third!

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.710
Safe!

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.880
Oh man!

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.700
Okay! Okay!

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.210
The third baseman sucks!

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.380
I see...

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:43.980
M-My bad... Shigeno...

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.850
M-My bad... Shigeno...

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.840
M-My bad... Shigeno...

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.180
D-Don't worry about it!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.770
Just remember our practice and calm down.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.020
<i>They got a runner on base already.</i>

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:58.980
Batting second: second baseman, Endo-kun.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.750
A sacrifice bunt from the very beginning, huh?

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:12.380
As usual, a person who memorizes the manual and doesn't have a mind of his own!

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:15.290
Second!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.380
No, first!

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.700
They're fast.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.590
W-Wait! Don't throw it!

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.250
W-Why's there no one there!?

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:29.630
Hey, what are you doing over here?

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:31.790
Fuji!

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:33.180
What the hell are you doing!?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.800
You're supposed to be covering first!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.480
My bad, my bad...

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.320
We didn't do anything and we've got runners on first and second.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.150
These guys are funny.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.650
Batting third: third baseman, Itou-kun.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.450
My, my... 

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:53.280
even though you're at such a low level, you actually scheduled an exhibition game with us...

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.960
Did you think that having such a pitcher is enough to play against us? 

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.510
That kind of makes me mad...

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:07.010
It'll get through...

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:09.550
What!?

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:12.470
Out!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.640
Out!

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.060
We did it!

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.060
All right!

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.480
Nice double play!

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.440
Did you see that? My awesome defense!

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.450
<i>He made it into his own accomplishment.</i>

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.250
Hey, aren't they hitting his pitches too easily?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.470
That kid... he's not serious yet.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:40.930
What?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.850
I thought they would all suck, but that shortstop seems pretty good.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.980
Yes, we are a low-level team.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:58.310
That's why we're having you guys help us with simulating fielding practice.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.530
Are you trying to say that you're letting us hit it on purpose?

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:08.860
If he threw seriously, there really wouldn't be any simulated fielding for us anymore.{it wouldn't really be simulating practice anymore...}

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.000
Batting fourth: center fielder, Aoyanagi-kun.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.060
Shigeno-kun isn't playing seriously?

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:22.950
Yeah.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.250
Even if it's our second string, 

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.590
in order to hit the fastballs that Shigeno pitches at full strength...

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.530
you need to go through the batting order at least once.

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:34.390
Foul!

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:38.390
And they're getting hit so easily,

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.410
but he's not even discouraged.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.820
It seems like Seishuu is planning something as well.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:54.030
<i>You can't strike them out, Nogoro-kun.</i>

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.410
Ball.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.250
What? That pitcher isn't pitching seriously?

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:07.580
Yeah, it seems as though they're letting us hit it so they can have simulated fielding practice.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.050
<i>Whether you pitch seriously or not; </i>

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.270
<i>either way, it doesn't matter...</i>

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.900
<i>Don't take me lightly!</i>

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.750
You guys haven't faced anyone scary, have you?

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.960
What is with his hair?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:54.450
If you guys are going to be like that, then we'll keep hitting them.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.740
Until you guys get serious, that is.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.870
<i>W-What!?</i>

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:17.330
<i>For the others' simulated fielding practice, don't strike them out!?</i>

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.310
<i>That's right.</i>

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.820
<i>No matter how many people you can strike out,</i>

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.870
<i>at this rate, the team won't get any stronger.</i>

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:29.290
<i>You're asking me to play a fixed game?</i>

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.890
<i>This is not an official game.</i>

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.310
<i>It is just an exhibition game.</i>

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:37.250
<i>If you can't do this...</i>

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:41.300
<i>I will cancel this game.</i>

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.680
<i>What'd you say!?</i>

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:51.550
This is a free fansub.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:51.550
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:21.930
All right! Fourth run!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.300
This isn't even fielding practice.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.550
It's just picking up balls.

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:35.030
Batting ninth: pitcher, Enomoto-kun.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.920
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.730
<i>Does Shigeno's pitching not work against even Kaido's second string?</i>

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:53.530
Damn!

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.290
I can't take it anymore.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:02.730
With runners on first and second...

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:04.810
He's winding up?

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:06.270
That idiot!

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.770
Don't get too cocky! 

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:11.730
Strike!

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.780
What was that pitch just now?

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:27.780
H-He... don't tell me...

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.990
H-He... don't tell me...

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:29.950
H-He... don't tell me...

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:33.540
He wasn't being serious up until now?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.450
Time!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.310
What's going on, Shigeno?

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.250
Have you forgotten what the coach said?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.390
You were told not to strike them out!

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.890
Shut up.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:46.600
They got four runs... As if I could keep doing that.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:51.800
Besides, if they're hitting so many,
this isn't even a proper simulation anymore.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:55.140
That's true, but the promise...

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.280
It's fine. Just go back.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.830
Once the game resumes, we'll be the ones controlling the game.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.330
<i>I don't care what happens...</i>

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:06.330
Two outs! Two outs!

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:08.880
I wonder what they were talking about.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.290
Who knows?

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.830
Strike!

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.420
<i>A gyroball, huh?</i>

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.280
<i>This guy... </i>

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:32.100
<i>he's increased his speed again?</i>

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:41.120
Strike! Batter out!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.420
Three outs! Change!

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.360
That was amazing, Shigeno!

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.350
You bastard... What were you doing up until now!?

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.590
You've broken our promise, haven't you, Nogoro-kun?

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.220
P-Promise?

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:02.760
What are you talking about?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.270
There's nothing I can do.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.810
I'll have them cancel this game.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.000
"C-Cancel"?

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.510
What's going on?

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.690
What are you talking about!?

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.630
The game that you worked so hard to schedule...

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:19.810
to cancel it now-

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.180
Shut up!

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.230
Enough already.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:28.900
I did not schedule this game to watch your one-man show!

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.010
Coach! 

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:37.380
For Shigeno not to hold back anymore, it's not unreasonable.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:41.120
It's no longer a simulation; it's more like Kaido's batting practice!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.550
Simulation practice?

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.590
Then... Shigeno was letting them hit on purpose?

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:51.610
But... those two outs... didn't you properly defend and get them?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.810
Yes, Nogoro-kun is a reliable pitcher.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:04.740
But, even so, to have him give us a piggyback ride all the way through,

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.900
high school baseball isn't that easy.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.130
The fielders...

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:11.200
have to defend with their own power.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:16.820
Nogoro-kun has to trust the fielders and let the opponent hit his pitches.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:23.330
Even if you lose by 10 runs, when you get 27 outs together as a team, 

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:27.970
Seishuu will finally become a true team.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:29.830
Excuse me...

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.550
The first batter is?

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.670
But...

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.390
if Nogoro-kun cannot follow my instructions,

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.960
there's nothing I can do.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.260
Excuse me, Umpire, about this game-

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.640
Wait a moment.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.540
I got it.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:46.410
The next 24 outs... I just have to allow them to hit and let everyone get them, right?

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.210
Excuse me... is there something wrong?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.600
Oh, nothing...

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.400
Nogoro-kun,

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.840
you're first in this inning, right?

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.290
But you know, old man...

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.950
A game where we lose and it's okay...

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.630
That's not in my vocabulary!

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:17.980
Play!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.330
All right! A home run on the first pitch! {Need Soda to note me all things said in the background}

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.130
Don't worry about it.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.650
Shigeno was good enough to come to our school.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:57.130
As long as we watch out for him, we should be okay.

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:13.010
Out!

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.440
Nice, Uchiyama!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.630
Out!

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:25.800
Nice, Noguchi!

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.950
All right, let's keep it going!

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.100
Yeah!

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.300
You guys...

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:42.680
We haven't been able to score any runs...

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.100
Batting first: shortstop, Shimizu-kun.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.530
All right, we're going to do great this inning!

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:51.820
Get on base, Taiga!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.500
All right!

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.460
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.730
Keep it going, Uchiyama!

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.960
D-Don't ask for the impossible.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.570
Strike!

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:17.790
How can I hit it?

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.480
Uchiyama-kun!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:23.430
You just need to do what you can do and that'll be fine.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.310
<i>What... I can do?</i>

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.750
<i>T-That's right.</i>

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:35.820
<i>The reason I'm batting second is...</i>

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:40.960
First!

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:43.660
Out!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.180
Nice one, Uchiyama-kun!

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:53.020
With a five run difference, a sacrifice bunt is nice? 

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.040
With these small achievements, 

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.580
everyone's confidence will rise,

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.010
and it'll become the team's major motivational power.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.550
All right!

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.100
We've got a runner on first and third!

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:12.240
Batting fourth: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:24.530
Out!

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:30.460
All right! We've got the second run back!

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.870
As expected, Shigeno...

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.570
It was just a sacrifice fly.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:35.880
No.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.150
This one run...

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.250
for Seishuu High School's baseball team...

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:44.620
is the first run that the entire team worked to get together and should be remembered.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.360
Three outs. Change.

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.970
They did better than expected.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:05.660
Yeah. It'd be good if they could move forward like this but...

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:09.090
Kamata, 

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:11.390
warm up your body.

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:11.910
Yes, sir.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:20.310
Out!

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:24.960
It seems they're finally getting used to it.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.010
And he too...

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:32.610
The fun of pitching like this and uniting as a team...

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:35.750
it should be an emotion that he has never felt before. 

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:37.410
Out!

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:40.000
All right!

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.370
Nice, Taiga!

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:46.670
Umpire! Pinch hitter.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:50.620
At this time, a pinch hitter?

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.230
<i>You did well... getting all the way here.</i>

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:06.880
<i>As expected of you.</i>

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:08.850
<i>But...</i>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:10.980
<i>It ends here!</i>

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.530
A push bunt?

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:16.980
Okay!

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.020
Throw it here!

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:52.300
S-Shigeno!

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:08.900
<i>Farewell... Koshien's star.</i>

00:24:40.550 --> 00:24:44.000
Having hurt my foot, entering the tournament has become impossible for me.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:48.500
Facing a tough situation, the team members try standing on their own two feet, using their own strength.

00:24:48.980 --> 00:24:52.170
Wait a minute! I haven't given up yet!

00:24:52.730 --> 00:24:53.880
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:55.050
The Missing Ace.

00:24:55.050 --> 00:24:57.480
Run to the stage of your dreams!
